Switching
=========

VLANs, trunks, EtherChannel, spanning tree, VTP and layer 2 security.

Arguments named interfaces accept a single name or an array. VLAN lists accept a number, an array or a string such as "10-20".

VLANs and access ports
----------------------

createVlans(name, vlans)
    { 10: "SALES" } or [10, 20]

deleteVlan(name, vlans)
    no vlan

setAccessPort(name, interfaces, vlan, options)
    Access mode and VLAN

assignPorts(name, { vlan: interfaces }, options)
    Several VLANs at once

setVoiceVlan(name, interfaces, vlan)
    switchport voice vlan

parkUnusedPorts(name, interfaces, vlan)
    Move to a black hole VLAN and shut down

addSvi(name, vlan, address, mask, description)
    interface VlanX with an address

setManagementIp(name, vlan, address, mask, gateway)
    SVI plus ip default-gateway

Access port options: voiceVlan, portfast, bpduguard, description.

    createVlans("S1", { 10: "SALES", 20: "IT", 99: "MGMT", 999: "PARKING" });
    assignPorts("S1", {
        10: ["FastEthernet0/1", "FastEthernet0/2"],
        20: ["FastEthernet0/3", "FastEthernet0/4"]
    }, { portfast: true, bpduguard: true });
    setManagementIp("S1", 99, "192.168.99.2/24", null, "192.168.99.1");
    parkUnusedPorts("S1", ["FastEthernet0/20", "FastEthernet0/21"], 999);

Trunks
------

setTrunkPort(name, interfaces, allowed, native, options)
    Trunk mode with allowed and native VLAN

setDtpMode(name, interfaces, mode)
    switchport mode dynamic desirable and friends

Options: encapsulation, nonegotiate. On multilayer switches switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q is added automatically. Some Packet Tracer versions reject it on a 3650; the rejected line is reported in the return value and the rest of the config still applies.

EtherChannel
------------

createEtherChannel(name, group, interfaces, mode, options)
    Bundle ports into Port-channelN

setEtherChannelLoadBalance(name, method)
    port-channel load-balance, method is checked against the IOS list

getEtherChannelLoadBalance(name)
    Reads the method back from show etherchannel load-balance

Load balance methods: src-mac, dst-mac, src-dst-mac, src-ip, dst-ip, src-dst-ip,
src-port, dst-port, src-dst-port.

Modes: active, passive (LACP), desirable, auto (PAgP), on. An unknown mode throws
and lists all five, because Packet Tracer would answer with a bare invalid status
for the channel-group line:

    Invalid EtherChannel mode: lacp. Valid modes are active, passive, desirable,
    auto, on. active (LACP, the other side must be active or passive), ...

The group number must be a whole number from 1 to 48. When the members are access
ports the Port-channel gets the same access VLAN, so the bundle behaves like the
ports it replaced.

Options: trunk, allowedVlans, nativeVlan, encapsulation, accessVlan, address and mask for a layer 3 channel.

    createEtherChannel("S1", 1, ["FastEthernet0/23", "FastEthernet0/24"], "active", { trunk: true });
    createEtherChannel("S2", 1, ["FastEthernet0/23", "FastEthernet0/24"], "passive", { trunk: true });

Spanning tree
-------------

setStpMode(name, mode)
    pvst or rapid-pvst (default)

setStpRoot(name, vlans, role)
    root primary or root secondary

setStpPriority(name, vlans, priority)
    Multiple of 4096

setStpPortCost(name, interface, cost, vlan)
    Port cost

enablePortfast(name, interfaces, bpduguard)
    PortFast, BPDU guard on by default

enablePortfastDefault(name, bpduguard)
    PortFast on every access port

VTP
---

configureVtp(name, options)
    domain, mode (server, client, transparent), password, version, pruning

Port security and DHCP snooping
-------------------------------

configurePortSecurity(name, interfaces, options)
    Port security on access ports

recoverErrDisabled(name, interfaces)
    shutdown then no shutdown

enableDhcpSnooping(name, vlans, trusted, options)
    DHCP snooping with trusted ports

enableArpInspection(name, vlans, trusted)
    Dynamic ARP inspection

Port security options: maximum (1), violation (shutdown, restrict, protect), sticky
(true), macs, agingTime, agingType (absolute, inactivity).

maximum must be a whole number from 1 to 1024 and macs must look like
aaaa.bbbb.cccc or aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff, otherwise the builder throws before anything
is sent. The builder also writes no switchport port-security first: Packet Tracer
keeps the maximum and violation values of an earlier run on the port, and without
the reset a second call with a smaller maximum silently keeps the old limit.

    configurePortSecurity("S1", "FastEthernet0/1", { maximum: 2, violation: "restrict" });

DHCP snooping options: untrusted ports, rateLimit (15), option82.

    configurePortSecurity("S1", ["FastEthernet0/1", "FastEthernet0/2"], { maximum: 2, violation: "restrict" });
    enableDhcpSnooping("S1", [10, 20], "GigabitEthernet0/1", { untrusted: ["FastEthernet0/1"], rateLimit: 10 });

Command builders
----------------

buildVlans(vlans) -> VLAN lines

buildAccessPorts(interfaces, vlan, options) -> Access port blocks

buildSvi(vlan, address, mask, description) -> SVI block

buildTrunkPorts(interfaces, allowed, native, options) -> Trunk blocks

buildEtherChannel(group, interfaces, mode, options) -> EtherChannel blocks

buildVtp(options) -> VTP lines

buildPortSecurity(interfaces, options) -> Port security blocks

buildDhcpSnooping(vlans, trusted, options) -> DHCP snooping lines
